2 JOHN

CH1

13
The children of your sister greet you.

12
I had many things to write to you but I do not wish to write with paper and ink but I hope to come to you and speak face to face so that our joy may be complete.

11
For the one who greets him shares in his evil works.

10
If anyone comes to you and does not bring this teaching do not receive him into your house and do not greet him.

9
Anyone who goes too far and does not abide in the teaching of Christ does not have God. The one who abides in the teaching has both the Father and the Son.

8
Watch yourselves that you do not lose what we have accomplished but that you may receive a full reward.

7
For many deceivers have gone out into the world those who do not confess Jesus Christ coming in the flesh. This is the deceiver and the antichrist.

6
And this is love that we walk according to His commandments. This is the commandment just as you have heard from the beginning that you should walk in it.

5
And now I ask you lady not as writing a new commandment to you but the one which we have had from the beginning that we love one another.

4
I rejoiced greatly because I found some of your children walking in truth just as we received commandment from the Father.

3
Grace, mercy, and peace will be with us from God the Father and from Jesus Christ the Son of the Father in truth and love.

2
Because of the truth that abides in us and will be with us forever.

1
The elder to the chosen lady and her children whom I love in truth and not only I but also all who know the truth.
